cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or the artifacts in this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Calibrated Temporal Smoke Detection: an edge-oriented benchmark of Kalman-HSV-CNN and temporal evidence models"
abstract: >-
  We present a reproducible benchmark for wildfire/smoke video detection on edge
  hardware. The benchmark compares a classical Kalman background model + HSV
  candidate extraction + small CNN pipeline with fixed temporal rules and with
  calibrated temporal models (GRU, causal TCN, probabilistic evidence accumulator).
  All splits are performed at video level to prevent frame leakage, and results
  are reported with video-level false alarms per hour, detection delay,
  calibration error, latency, and energy per frame.
type: software
